+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers currently create orders and pay the full amount; there is no way to
+reduce what they owe. The `orders.discount_cents`, `orders.final_amount_cents`,
+`orders.coupon_code`, `coupons`, and `coupon_redemptions` structures already
+exist, but nothing reads or writes them. This change adds the missing behavior
+so a customer can apply one coupon to an order before paying.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- Normalize `couponCode` (trim, uppercase) before lookup (REQ-01).
+- Validate the order (exists, `PENDING`) and the coupon (exists, `ACTIVE`,
+  in its validity window, not usage-exhausted, order amount meets the minimum),
+  returning the documented error codes in the documented order.
+- Compute the discount for `FIXED` and `PERCENT` coupons, applying the optional
+  `maxDiscountCents` cap and clamping to the order amount; `finalAmountCents`
+  is never negative.
+- Persist the result atomically: update the order (`discount_cents`,
+  `final_amount_cents`, normalized `coupon_code`), insert a `coupon_redemptions`
+  row, and increment `coupons.used_count` in a single transaction; roll back on
+  any failure.
+- Return HTTP 200 with the updated order in the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`.
+- An order may use at most one coupon; a `PENDING` order's `status` is unchanged
+  by applying a coupon.
+
+Out of scope: removing or changing an applied coupon, coupon stacks, and any
+change to the database schema or existing endpoints.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupon`: Applying a single coupon to a pending order, including
+  discount calculation, validation/error semantics, and atomic redemption
+  bookkeeping.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- API: new `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` route on the existing order router.
+- Code: `routes/orders.ts` (route only), `services/orderService.ts` (all rules),
+  `repositories/orderRepository.ts` and `repositories/couponRepository.ts`
+  (SQL, including the transaction), and `app.ts` wiring so the order service can
+  reach the coupon repository.
+- Data: no schema changes; reuses `orders`, `coupons`, `coupon_redemptions`.
+- Dependencies: none added.
