+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Wiring and repository support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Update `createApp` in `src/app.ts` so `OrderService` receives the existing `CouponRepository` alongside `OrderRepository` and `Clock`; verify `npm run build` type-checks and the existing suite still passes with `npm test`.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon({ orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, now })` in `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` that runs the order update, `coupon_redemptions` insert, and `coupons.used_count + 1` inside one `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`/`COMMIT` block with `ROLLBACK` on error; verify in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` that success writes all three rows and a forced failure leaves no changes.
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` normalization and the section-6 validation order (INVALID_REQUEST, ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_NOT_PENDING, COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED, COUPON_NOT_FOUND, COUPON_INACTIVE, COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID, COUPON_EXPIRED, COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED, MINIMUM_NOT_MET) using `this.clock()`; verify with tests asserting each code and its precedence (AC-08, AC-10, error-table order).
+- [x] 2.2 Implement the discount math (FIXED value, PERCENT `floor(amount*value/100)`, optional cap, clamp to amount; `finalAmountCents = amount - discount`); verify with tests covering AC-01 through AC-06.
+- [x] 2.3 Verify boundary and no-side-effect behavior via tests: `now == validFrom` succeeds, `now == validUntil` is `COUPON_EXPIRED` (AC-07), and every rejection leaves the order amounts and `coupons.used_count` unchanged with no new redemption row.
+
+## 3. Route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` delegating to `OrderService.applyCoupon`; verify with tests that a successful call returns HTTP 200 with a body equal to the subsequent `GET /orders/:id`, that rejected calls use the `{ error: { code, message } }` shape, and that a success increments `usedCount` and adds one redemption row (AC-09, AC-14).
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both succeed, including the untouched existing tests, before considering the change complete.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after implementation and verification are complete.
